Carl wrote:
> Any chance you'll be supporting telnet this year? (I hope)

That's a tough one.  Is there any reason you'd need telnet instead of 
ssh?  Are there actually networks out there filtering ssh? (And would 
you really want to expose login credentials to the operaters of a 
network like that?)

The real reason for dropping telnet off our own servers was that OpenBSD 
seems to have stopped distributing it as part of the core OS, so it's a 
pain to even get a daemon onto the servers anymore.  We are open to 
supporting it (at least on a few servers) if someone can explain why we 
should ... ;-)

(Not being snarky; I've just never encountered a situation where telnet 
was available but ssh wasn't.)

